<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#A1.S6" title="In Appendix A Parallelism in Polar Spectral Operators ‣ Foundations of Polar Linear Algebra A Structured Framework for Radial–Angular Operators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.6 </span>Summary Table</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#A1.S7" title="In Appendix A Parallelism in Polar Spectral Operators ‣ Foundations of Polar Linear Algebra A Structured Framework for Radial–Angular Operators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.7 </span>Concluding Remarks</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_bibliography"><a href="#bib" title="In Foundations of Polar Linear Algebra A Structured Framework for Radial–Angular Operators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">References</span></a></li>
</ol></nav>
</section>
<section id="Ch1" class="ltx_chapter">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_chapter"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_chapter">Chapter 1 </span>Introduction to Polar Linear Algebra</h2>

<div id="Ch1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce a linear–algebraic framework for data defined over polar grids.
This chapter formalizes polar matrices, convolutional (circular) products, the polar transpose,
self-adjoint operators, norms, and the invertibility criterion known as Aurora’s Theorem.
Numerical examples and visual illustrations accompany each definition.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ch1.S1" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1.1 </span>Introduction</h3>

<div id="Ch1.S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Many natural and artificial signals possess inherent rotational symmetry:
fruit cross-sections, microphone arrays, radar sweeps, and circular patterns.
These structures are often more naturally represented on a polar grid than on a Cartesian one.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#Ch1.F1" title="Figure 1.1 ‣ 1.1 Introduction ‣ Chapter 1 Introduction to Polar Linear Algebra ‣ Foundations of Polar Linear Algebra A Structured Framework for Radial–Angular Operators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> shows a pomegranate cross-section, where
radial levels and angular sectors emerge organically from the physical morphology.
This motivates the introduction of <em id="Ch1.S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">polar matrices</em>,
operators indexed by radius <math id="Ch1.S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and angle <math id="Ch1.S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A[r,\theta],\quad r=0,\dots,N_{r}-1,\quad\theta=0,\dots,N_{\theta}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A[r,\theta],\quad r=0,\dots,N_{r}-1,\quad\theta=0,\dots,N_{\theta}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="Ch1.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.28939v1/figures/pomegranate.JPG" id="Ch1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/161;" width="215" height="161" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1.1: </span>A natural example of polar symmetry: a pomegranate cross-section.
Radial layers and angular segmentation align with a polar grid.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Ch1.S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Polar matrices form a structured algebra where the angular dimension
is governed by circular convolution and the radial dimension acts as
a collection of independent channels.
This chapter develops the fundamental algebraic properties of polar operators,
their symmetries, and their relevance for constructing rotation–equivariant
deep learning architectures.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notational and Conceptual Conventions.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this work, we distinguish between <em id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">polar matrices</em>
and <em id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">classical (linear) matrices</em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A <em id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">polar matrix</em> is a tensor indexed by radial and angular
coordinates and is combined with other polar matrices through the
<em id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">polar product</em> <math id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as circular convolution along
the angular dimension.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Classical matrices act on vectors via standard matrix multiplication.
Whenever classical linear operators are introduced (e.g. circulant
matrices or Fourier matrices), they will be explicitly referred to as
such. No ambiguity between polar operators and classical linear
operators is intended.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We distinguish between:
(i) operators acting on polar matrices (such as rotors),
(ii) the polar product <math id="Ch1.S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math> between polar matrices,
and (iii) classical matrix multiplication, which is only used
when explicitly stated.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S2" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1.2 </span>The Polar Grid and Polar Matrices</h3>

<div id="Ch1.S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A polar grid consists of discrete radii <math id="Ch1.S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and angular samples <math id="Ch1.S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\theta_{j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\theta_{j}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="Ch1.footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            The same design pattern extends naturally to tensors with more than one
angular dimension, such as

<span id="Ch1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A[r,\theta_{1},\theta_{2}]\in\mathbb{R}^{N_{r}\times N_{\theta_{1}}\times N_{\theta_{2}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A[r,\theta_{1},\theta_{2}]\in\mathbb{R}^{N_{r}\times N_{\theta_{1}}\times N_{\theta_{2}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="Ch1.S2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">polar matrix</span> is a tensor:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{N_{r}\times N_{\theta}},\qquad A[r,\theta]=\text{value at sector }(r,\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>value at sector </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{N_{r}\times N_{\theta}},\qquad A[r,\theta]=\text{value at sector }(r,\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="Ch1.S2.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Example: a simple polar matrix</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S2.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S2.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Ch1.S2.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{r}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{r}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ch1.S2.SSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\theta}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\theta}=4</annotation></semantics></math>.
A simple polar matrix is represented in figure <a href="#Ch1.F2" title="Figure 1.2 ‣ Example: a simple polar matrix ‣ 1.2 The Polar Grid and Polar Matrices ‣ Chapter 1 Introduction to Polar Linear Algebra ‣ Foundations of Polar Linear Algebra A Structured Framework for Radial–Angular Operators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S2.SSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S2.SSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Row <math id="Ch1.S2.SSx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the inner ring, row <math id="Ch1.S2.SSx1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=1</annotation></semantics></math> to the outer ring; columns represent equally spaced angles.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ch1.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.28939v1/figures/polar_matrix_example.png" id="Ch1.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:215/190;" width="215" height="190" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1.2: </span>A polar matrix represented in its natural radial–angular form.
The inner ring contains the values <math id="Ch1.F2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,1,0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,1,0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and the outer ring the values <math id="Ch1.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3,2,1,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3,2,1,0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S2.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Cartesian representation of a polar matrix (counterclockwise <math id="Ch1.S2.SSx2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>)</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S2.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S2.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In polar coordinates we adopt the standard mathematical convention:
<math id="Ch1.S2.SSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> increases counterclockwise, with <math id="Ch1.S2.SSx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=0</annotation></semantics></math> on the positive <math id="Ch1.S2.SSx2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>–axis.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S2.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S2.SSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Under this indexing, the polar matrix shown in Fig. <a href="#Ch1.F2" title="Figure 1.2 ‣ Example: a simple polar matrix ‣ 1.2 The Polar Grid and Polar Matrices ‣ Chapter 1 Introduction to Polar Linear Algebra ‣ Foundations of Polar Linear Algebra A Structured Framework for Radial–Angular Operators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>
corresponds to the Cartesian form</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;1&amp;0&amp;1\\
3&amp;2&amp;1&amp;0\end{pmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;1&amp;0&amp;1\\
3&amp;2&amp;1&amp;0\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S2.SSx2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where rows represent radial levels and columns represent angular samples
<math id="Ch1.S2.SSx2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\tfrac{\pi}{2},\pi,\tfrac{3\pi}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\tfrac{\pi}{2},\pi,\tfrac{3\pi}{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The first row corresponds to the inner radial level, while the second row
represents the outer level, with columns ordered cyclically along the angular dimension.
This Cartesian form is often convenient for algebraic manipulation,
while preserving the underlying polar semantics.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S3" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1.3 </span>Algebra on Polar Matrices</h3>

<div id="Ch1.S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we define the basic algebraic operations on polar matrices:
addition, scalar multiplication, Hadamard product, polar product, polar transpose,
self-adjointness, and inner product/norm.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ch1.S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.3.1 </span>Addition</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given two polar matrices <math id="Ch1.S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B\in\mathbb{R}^{N_{r}\times N_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B\in\mathbb{R}^{N_{r}\times N_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, their sum is defined pointwise:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A+B)[r,\theta]=A[r,\theta]+B[r,\theta]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A+B)[r,\theta]=A[r,\theta]+B[r,\theta].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S3.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Example</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S3.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S3.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;2&amp;3&amp;4\\
2&amp;0&amp;1&amp;3\end{pmatrix},\quad B=\begin{pmatrix}4&amp;3&amp;2&amp;1\\
1&amp;1&amp;1&amp;1\end{pmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;2&amp;3&amp;4\\
2&amp;0&amp;1&amp;3\end{pmatrix},\quad B=\begin{pmatrix}4&amp;3&amp;2&amp;1\\
1&amp;1&amp;1&amp;1\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S3.SSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">we have</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+B=\begin{pmatrix}5&amp;5&amp;5&amp;5\\
3&amp;1&amp;2&amp;4\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>5</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>5</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>5</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>5</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+B=\begin{pmatrix}5&amp;5&amp;5&amp;5\\
3&amp;1&amp;2&amp;4\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.3.2 </span>Scalar multiplication</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any scalar <math id="Ch1.S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the scalar–polar matrix product is defined by</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda A)[r,\theta]=\lambda\,A[r,\theta]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda A)[r,\theta]=\lambda\,A[r,\theta].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S3.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Example</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S3.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S3.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Ch1.S3.SSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=3</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;2&amp;3&amp;4\\
2&amp;0&amp;1&amp;3\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;2&amp;3&amp;4\\
2&amp;0&amp;1&amp;3\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S3.SSx2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3A=\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;6&amp;9&amp;12\\
6&amp;0&amp;3&amp;9\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>6</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>9</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>12</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>6</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>9</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3A=\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;6&amp;9&amp;12\\
6&amp;0&amp;3&amp;9\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.3.3 </span>Hadamard (elementwise) product</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given two polar matrices A,B the elementwise product (Hadamard product) is</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A\odot B)[r,\theta]=A[r,\theta]\,B[r,\theta]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A\odot B)[r,\theta]=A[r,\theta]\,B[r,\theta].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S4" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1.4 </span>The Polar Product (Circular Convolution)</h3>

<div id="Ch1.S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The key operation in polar linear algebra is the <span id="Ch1.S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">polar product</span>, defined as angular circular convolution at each radius.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given two polar matrices A,B, for each radius <math id="Ch1.S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, define:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A\otimes B)[r,\theta]=\sum_{k=0}^{N_{\theta}-1}A[r,k]\,B[r,(\theta-k)\bmod N_{\theta}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A\otimes B)[r,\theta]=\sum_{k=0}^{N_{\theta}-1}A[r,k]\,B[r,(\theta-k)\bmod N_{\theta}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This is just circular convolution of the angular vectors <math id="Ch1.S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A[r,:]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A[r,:]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ch1.S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B[r,:]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B[r,:]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ch1.S4.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Example 1: circular convolution on a single ring</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S4.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S4.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let at a fixed radius <math id="Ch1.S4.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=[2,1,0,1],\quad b=[1,0,1,0]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=[2,1,0,1],\quad b=[1,0,1,0].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S4.SSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a\otimes b)[0]=2\cdot 1+1\cdot 0+0\cdot 1+1\cdot 0=2," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a\otimes b)[0]=2\cdot 1+1\cdot 0+0\cdot 1+1\cdot 0=2,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="Ch1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a\otimes b)[1]=2\cdot 0+1\cdot 1+0\cdot 0+1\cdot 1=2," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a\otimes b)[1]=2\cdot 0+1\cdot 1+0\cdot 0+1\cdot 1=2,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S4.SSx1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and similarly one checks that</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\otimes b=[2,2,2,2]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\otimes b=[2,2,2,2].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S4.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Example 2: circular product of two <math id="Ch1.S4.SSx2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> polar matrices</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S4.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S4.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;1&amp;0\\
3&amp;2&amp;1\end{pmatrix},\qquad B=\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0&amp;1\\
2&amp;1&amp;0\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;1&amp;0\\
3&amp;2&amp;1\end{pmatrix},\qquad B=\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0&amp;1\\
2&amp;1&amp;0\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S4.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S4.SSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each radius <math id="Ch1.S4.SSx2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, the circular convolution is</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A\otimes B)[r,\theta]=\sum_{k=0}^{2}A[r,k]\;B[r,(\theta-k)\bmod 3]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A\otimes B)[r,\theta]=\sum_{k=0}^{2}A[r,k]\;B[r,(\theta-k)\bmod 3].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S4.SSx2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S4.SSx2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Computing row by row:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(A\otimes B)[0,:]=[3,\;1,\;2],\qquad(A\otimes B)[1,:]=[7,\;7,\;4]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 4</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A\otimes B)[0,:]=[3,\;1,\;2],\qquad(A\otimes B)[1,:]=[7,\;7,\;4],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S4.SSx2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">so that</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\otimes B=\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;1&amp;2\\
7&amp;7&amp;4\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>7</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>7</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\otimes B=\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;1&amp;2\\
7&amp;7&amp;4\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S5" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1.5 </span>Polar Transpose</h3>

<div id="Ch1.S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="Ch1.S5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">polar transpose</span> reflects the angular index:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{T_{p}}[r,\theta]=A[r,(-\theta)\bmod N_{\theta}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{T_{p}}[r,\theta]=A[r,(-\theta)\bmod N_{\theta}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, this corresponds to mirroring the pattern in <math id="Ch1.S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ch1.S5.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Example</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S5.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S5.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="Ch1.S5.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=[2,1,0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=[2,1,0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{T_{p}}=[2,1,0,1]\quad\text{(same, because symmetric)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(same, because symmetric)</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{T_{p}}=[2,1,0,1]\quad\text{(same, because symmetric)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S5.SSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">But if <math id="Ch1.S5.SSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=[5,4,3,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=[5,4,3,2]</annotation></semantics></math>, then:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{T_{p}}=[5,2,3,4]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{T_{p}}=[5,2,3,4].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S6" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1.6 </span>Self-Adjoint Polar Matrices</h3>

<div id="Ch1.S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let
<math id="Ch1.S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{C}^{N_{r}\times N_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{C}^{N_{r}\times N_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>
be a complex-valued polar matrix.
We define the <em id="Ch1.S6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">polar adjoint</em> as</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A^{\dagger_{p}}[r,\theta]=\overline{A[r,(-\theta)\bmod N_{\theta}]}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\dagger_{p}}[r,\theta]=\overline{A[r,(-\theta)\bmod N_{\theta}]},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the overline denotes complex conjugation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A polar matrix is said to be <em id="Ch1.S6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">self-adjoint</em> if</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A=A^{\dagger_{p}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=A^{\dagger_{p}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="Ch1.S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remark (Real-valued case).</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="Ch1.S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is real-valued, complex conjugation is trivial and the polar adjoint
reduces to the polar transpose:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A^{\dagger_{p}}=A^{T_{p}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\dagger_{p}}=A^{T_{p}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In this case, self-adjoint polar matrices coincide with
<em id="Ch1.S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">polar-symmetric</em> matrices, satisfying</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A[r,\theta]=A[r,-\theta]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A[r,\theta]=A[r,-\theta].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S6.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Example</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S6.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S6.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Ch1.S6.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\theta}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\theta}=4</annotation></semantics></math>, the condition requires:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A[r,1]=A[r,3],\quad A[r,0]\text{ arbitrary},\quad A[r,2]\text{ arbitrary}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> arbitrary</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> arbitrary</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A[r,1]=A[r,3],\quad A[r,0]\text{ arbitrary},\quad A[r,2]\text{ arbitrary}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S6.SSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This corresponds to angular symmetry around <math id="Ch1.S6.SSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S7" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1.7 </span>Inner Product and Norm</h3>

<div id="Ch1.S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define the inner product between two polar matrices as the Frobenius inner product:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle A,B\rangle=\sum_{r=0}^{N_{r}-1}\sum_{\theta=0}^{N_{\theta}-1}A[r,\theta]\,B[r,\theta]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle A,B\rangle=\sum_{r=0}^{N_{r}-1}\sum_{\theta=0}^{N_{\theta}-1}A[r,\theta]\,B[r,\theta],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the corresponding norm:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A\|=\sqrt{\langle A,A\rangle}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A\|=\sqrt{\langle A,A\rangle}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="Ch1.S7.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Example</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S7.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;2\\
3&amp;4\end{pmatrix}\Rightarrow\|A\|=\sqrt{1^{2}+2^{2}+3^{2}+4^{2}}=\sqrt{30}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>30</mn></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;2\\
3&amp;4\end{pmatrix}\Rightarrow\|A\|=\sqrt{1^{2}+2^{2}+3^{2}+4^{2}}=\sqrt{30}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S8" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1.8 </span>Fourier View on Polar Operators</h3>

<div id="Ch1.S8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since the polar product is circular convolution in the angular dimension, it is natural to analyze polar matrices in the angular Fourier domain.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Ch1.S8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of angular samples of a polar matrix <math id="Ch1.S8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. For a fixed radius <math id="Ch1.S8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the angular vector</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a[\theta]=A[r,\theta],\qquad\theta=0,\dots,N_{\theta}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a[\theta]=A[r,\theta],\qquad\theta=0,\dots,N_{\theta}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S8.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Its discrete Fourier transform (DFT) is</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{a}[m]=\sum_{\theta=0}^{N_{\theta}-1}a[\theta]\;e^{-i2\pi m\theta/N_{\theta}},\qquad m=0,\dots,N_{\theta}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[m]=\sum_{\theta=0}^{N_{\theta}-1}a[\theta]\;e^{-i2\pi m\theta/N_{\theta}},\qquad m=0,\dots,N_{\theta}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The key property is that circular convolution becomes pointwise multiplication in the Fourier domain:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a\otimes b)[\theta]\;\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{DFT}}}{{\longleftrightarrow}}\;\hat{a}[m]\,\hat{b}[m]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mover><mo stretchy="false">⟷</mo><mtext>DFT</mtext></mover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a\otimes b)[\theta]\;\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{DFT}}}{{\longleftrightarrow}}\;\hat{a}[m]\,\hat{b}[m].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S8.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This is the spectral backbone of Aurora’s Theorem.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S9" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1.9 </span>Aurora’s Theorem</h3>

<div id="Ch1.S9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Ch1.S9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}[r,m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}[r,m]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the discrete Fourier transform (DFT) of
<math id="Ch1.S9.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A[r,:]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A[r,:]</annotation></semantics></math> along the angular dimension, with frequency index
<math id="Ch1.S9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathbb{Z}_{N_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathbb{Z}_{N_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.1</span></span><span id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Aurora’s Theorem (Invertibility Criterion))<span id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A polar matrix <math id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible under the polar product <math id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if</span></p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}[r,m]\neq 0\quad\text{for all radii $r$ and all frequencies $m$}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all radii </mtext><mi>r</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and all frequencies </mtext><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}[r,m]\neq 0\quad\text{for all radii $r$ and all frequencies $m$}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In that case the inverse is uniquely given by</span></p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{-1}[r,\theta]=\mathcal{F}^{-1}_{\theta}\!\left(\frac{1}{\hat{A}[r,m]}\right)[\theta]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1}[r,\theta]=\mathcal{F}^{-1}_{\theta}\!\left(\frac{1}{\hat{A}[r,m]}\right)[\theta],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(i.e.,  at each radius <math id="Ch1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> we invert the angular spectrum and apply the inverse DFT).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S9.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Ch1.S9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch1.S9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix a radius <math id="Ch1.S9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and define the angular vector</span></p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a[\theta]=A[r,\theta],\qquad\theta=0,\dots,N_{\theta}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a[\theta]=A[r,\theta],\qquad\theta=0,\dots,N_{\theta}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S9.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch1.S9.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">For this fixed radius, the polar product reduces to circular convolution:</span></p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a\otimes b)[\theta]=\sum_{k=0}^{N_{\theta}-1}a[k]\,b[(\theta-k)\bmod N_{\theta}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a\otimes b)[\theta]=\sum_{k=0}^{N_{\theta}-1}a[k]\,b[(\theta-k)\bmod N_{\theta}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S9.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ch1.S9.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The identity vector is the angular Kronecker delta</span></p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta[\theta]=\begin{cases}1&amp;\theta=0,\\
0&amp;\theta\neq 0.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta[\theta]=\begin{cases}1&amp;\theta=0,\\
0&amp;\theta\neq 0.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Necessity.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume that <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible under <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. so that there exists <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\otimes A^{-1}=I." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\otimes A^{-1}=I.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For the fixed radius <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> this means that there exists <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\otimes b=\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\otimes b=\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We denote by <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}[m]=\hat{A}[r,m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[m]=\hat{A}[r,m]</annotation></semantics></math> the DFT of the angular profile
at fixed radius <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying the DFT in the angular dimension and using the convolution–multiplication property, we obtain</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{a\otimes b}[m]=\hat{a}[m]\,\hat{b}[m]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{a\otimes b}[m]=\hat{a}[m]\,\hat{b}[m].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, the DFT of the delta vector is constant:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\delta}[m]=1\quad\forall m." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\delta}[m]=1\quad\forall m.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}[m]\,\hat{b}[m]=1\quad\forall m," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[m]\,\hat{b}[m]=1\quad\forall m,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which immediately implies <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}[m]\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[m]\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sufficiency.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Conversely, assume that <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}[m]\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[m]\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for every frequency index <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{b}[m]=\frac{1}{\hat{a}[m]}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{b}[m]=\frac{1}{\hat{a}[m]},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and let <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> be the inverse DFT of <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{b}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b[\theta]=\mathcal{F}^{-1}(\hat{b})[\theta]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b[\theta]=\mathcal{F}^{-1}(\hat{b})[\theta].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{a\otimes b}[m]=\hat{a}[m]\hat{b}[m]=\hat{a}[m]\frac{1}{\hat{a}[m]}=1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{a\otimes b}[m]=\hat{a}[m]\hat{b}[m]=\hat{a}[m]\frac{1}{\hat{a}[m]}=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">so that <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\otimes b=\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\otimes b=\delta</annotation></semantics></math> after applying the inverse DFT. Thus <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> is the inverse of <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> under circular convolution for that radius.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Global statement.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since the argument holds independently for each radius <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, the polar
matrix <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible under <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if
<math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}[r,m]\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}[r,m]\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.
The inverse is obtained independently at each radius by pointwise
inversion in the angular Fourier domain:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{-1}[r,\theta]=\mathcal{F}^{-1}_{\theta}\!\left(\frac{1}{\hat{A}[r,m]}\right)[\theta]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1}[r,\theta]=\mathcal{F}^{-1}_{\theta}\!\left(\frac{1}{\hat{A}[r,m]}\right)[\theta].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Although the explicit computation of the inverse operator is rarely required in
modern learning pipelines, the notion of invertibility plays a crucial role in
understanding information preservation, numerical stability, and gradient
propagation. Aurora’s Theorem therefore provides a structural guarantee rather
than an operational recipe, ensuring that polar convolution operators do not
collapse relevant subspaces of the signal.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1.10 </span>Numerical Examples for Aurora’s Theorem</h3>

<div id="Ch1.S10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now illustrate Aurora’s Theorem with explicit DFT computations for <math id="Ch1.S10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\theta}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\theta}=4</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\omega=e^{-i2\pi/4}=e^{-i\pi/2}=-i,\qquad\omega^{0}=1,\;\omega^{1}=-i,\;\omega^{2}=-1,\;\omega^{3}=i." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>ω</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>ω</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>ω</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>ω</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=e^{-i2\pi/4}=e^{-i\pi/2}=-i,\qquad\omega^{0}=1,\;\omega^{1}=-i,\;\omega^{2}=-1,\;\omega^{3}=i.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Example 1: a non-invertible polar filter</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the angular vector</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=[1,0,1,0]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=[1,0,1,0].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We compute its DFT componentwise:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}[m]=\sum_{n=0}^{3}a[n]\,\omega^{mn}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[m]=\sum_{n=0}^{3}a[n]\,\omega^{mn}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Coefficient <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch1.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}[0]=1+0+1+0=2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[0]=1+0+1+0=2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Coefficient <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch1.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}[1]=1\cdot\omega^{0}+0\cdot\omega^{1}+1\cdot\omega^{2}+0\cdot\omega^{3}=1+0-1+0=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[1]=1\cdot\omega^{0}+0\cdot\omega^{1}+1\cdot\omega^{2}+0\cdot\omega^{3}=1+0-1+0=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Coefficient <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{2n}=[1,-1,1,-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{2n}=[1,-1,1,-1]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}[2]=1\cdot 1+0\cdot(-1)+1\cdot 1+0\cdot(-1)=2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[2]=1\cdot 1+0\cdot(-1)+1\cdot 1+0\cdot(-1)=2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Coefficient <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=3</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{3n}=[1,i,-1,-i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{3n}=[1,i,-1,-i]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}[3]=1\cdot 1+0\cdot i+1\cdot(-1)+0\cdot(-i)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[3]=1\cdot 1+0\cdot i+1\cdot(-1)+0\cdot(-i)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Result.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch1.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}=[2,\,0,\,2,\,0]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}=[2,\,0,\,2,\,0].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two frequency components vanish, hence by Aurora’s Theorem
the filter is <span id="Ch1.S10.SSx1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">not invertible</span> under circular convolution.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Example 2: an invertible polar filter</h4>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider now</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=[2,1,1,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=[2,1,1,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Coefficient <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch1.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}[0]=2+1+1+1=5." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[0]=2+1+1+1=5.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Coefficient <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch1.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}[1]=2\cdot 1+1\cdot(-i)+1\cdot(-1)+1\cdot i=2-i-1+i=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[1]=2\cdot 1+1\cdot(-i)+1\cdot(-1)+1\cdot i=2-i-1+i=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Coefficient <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{2n}=[1,-1,1,-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{2n}=[1,-1,1,-1]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}[2]=2\cdot 1+1\cdot(-1)+1\cdot 1+1\cdot(-1)=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[2]=2\cdot 1+1\cdot(-1)+1\cdot 1+1\cdot(-1)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Coefficient <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=3</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{3n}=[1,i,-1,-i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{3n}=[1,i,-1,-i]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}[3]=2\cdot 1+1\cdot i+1\cdot(-1)+1\cdot(-i)=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}[3]=2\cdot 1+1\cdot i+1\cdot(-1)+1\cdot(-i)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Result.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ch1.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}=[5,\,1,\,1,\,1]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}=[5,\,1,\,1,\,1],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">all nonzero.
Hence the filter is <span id="Ch1.S10.SSx2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">invertible</span> under convolution, with inverse</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{-1}=\mathcal{F}^{-1}\!\left(\frac{1}{\hat{a}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{-1}=\mathcal{F}^{-1}\!\left(\frac{1}{\hat{a}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Worked example: explicit computation of <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{-1}=\mathcal{F}^{-1}(1/\hat{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{-1}=\mathcal{F}^{-1}(1/\hat{a})</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We continue Example 2 with the invertible filter</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=[2,1,1,1],\quad\hat{a}=[5,1,1,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=[2,1,1,1],\quad\hat{a}=[5,1,1,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Constructing <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\hat{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\hat{a}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{b}[m]=\frac{1}{\hat{a}[m]},\qquad m=0,1,2,3," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{b}[m]=\frac{1}{\hat{a}[m]},\qquad m=0,1,2,3,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so that</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{b}=\Bigl[\,0.2,\;1,\;1,\;1\,\Bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mn> 0.2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{b}=\Bigl[\,0.2,\;1,\;1,\;1\,\Bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Inverse DFT formula.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compute</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="b[n]=\mathcal{F}^{-1}(\hat{b})[n],\qquad n=0,1,2,3." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b[n]=\mathcal{F}^{-1}(\hat{b})[n],\qquad n=0,1,2,3.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">With the standard IDFT convention for <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=4</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b[n]=\frac{1}{4}\sum_{m=0}^{3}\hat{b}[m]\;e^{i2\pi mn/4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b[n]=\frac{1}{4}\sum_{m=0}^{3}\hat{b}[m]\;e^{i2\pi mn/4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=e^{i2\pi/4}=e^{i\pi/2}=i," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=e^{i2\pi/4}=e^{i\pi/2}=i,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">so that</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{0}=1,\quad\omega^{1}=i,\quad\omega^{2}=-1,\quad\omega^{3}=-i." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{0}=1,\quad\omega^{1}=i,\quad\omega^{2}=-1,\quad\omega^{3}=-i.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Coefficient <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b[0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b[0]</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0</annotation></semantics></math> all complex exponentials are equal to <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{i2\pi m\cdot 0/4}=1\quad\forall m." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{i2\pi m\cdot 0/4}=1\quad\forall m.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b[0]=\frac{1}{4}\bigl(0.2+1+1+1\bigr)=\frac{3.2}{4}=0.8." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3.2</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b[0]=\frac{1}{4}\bigl(0.2+1+1+1\bigr)=\frac{3.2}{4}=0.8.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 4: Coefficient <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b[1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b[1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math> we have the factors</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{i2\pi m\cdot 1/4}=\omega^{m}\in\{1,i,-1,-i\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{i2\pi m\cdot 1/4}=\omega^{m}\in\{1,i,-1,-i\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch1.Ex74X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex74X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b[1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b[1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex74X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\Bigl(\hat{b}[0]\omega^{0}+\hat{b}[1]\omega^{1}+\hat{b}[2]\omega^{2}+\hat{b}[3]\omega^{3}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\Bigl(\hat{b}[0]\omega^{0}+\hat{b}[1]\omega^{1}+\hat{b}[2]\omega^{2}+\hat{b}[3]\omega^{3}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch1.Ex74Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex74Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\Bigl(0.2\cdot 1+1\cdot i+1\cdot(-1)+1\cdot(-i)\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\Bigl(0.2\cdot 1+1\cdot i+1\cdot(-1)+1\cdot(-i)\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch1.Ex74Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex74Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{-0.8}{4}=-0.2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{-0.8}{4}=-0.2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 5: Coefficient <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b[2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b[2]</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math> we need the terms <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{2m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{2m}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{2\cdot 0}=1,\quad\omega^{2\cdot 1}=\omega^{2}=-1,\quad\omega^{2\cdot 2}=\omega^{4}=1,\quad\omega^{2\cdot 3}=\omega^{6}=\omega^{2}=-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{2\cdot 0}=1,\quad\omega^{2\cdot 1}=\omega^{2}=-1,\quad\omega^{2\cdot 2}=\omega^{4}=1,\quad\omega^{2\cdot 3}=\omega^{6}=\omega^{2}=-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch1.Ex76X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex76X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b[2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b[2]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex76X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\Bigl(0.2\cdot 1+1\cdot(-1)+1\cdot 1+1\cdot(-1)\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\Bigl(0.2\cdot 1+1\cdot(-1)+1\cdot 1+1\cdot(-1)\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch1.Ex76Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex76Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{-0.8}{4}=-0.2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{-0.8}{4}=-0.2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 6: Coefficient <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b[3]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b[3]</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3</annotation></semantics></math> we need the terms <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{3m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{3m}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{3\cdot 0}=1,\quad\omega^{3\cdot 1}=\omega^{3}=-i,\quad\omega^{3\cdot 2}=\omega^{6}=\omega^{2}=-1,\quad\omega^{3\cdot 3}=\omega^{9}=\omega^{1}=i." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{3\cdot 0}=1,\quad\omega^{3\cdot 1}=\omega^{3}=-i,\quad\omega^{3\cdot 2}=\omega^{6}=\omega^{2}=-1,\quad\omega^{3\cdot 3}=\omega^{9}=\omega^{1}=i.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">So</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch1.Ex78X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex78X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b[3]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b[3]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex78X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\Bigl(0.2\cdot 1+1\cdot(-i)+1\cdot(-1)+1\cdot i\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\Bigl(0.2\cdot 1+1\cdot(-i)+1\cdot(-1)+1\cdot i\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch1.Ex78Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex78Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{-0.8}{4}=-0.2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{-0.8}{4}=-0.2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 7: Resulting inverse filter.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have obtained</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{-1}=b=[\,0.8,\,-0.2,\,-0.2,\,-0.2\,]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn> 0.8</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{-1}=b=[\,0.8,\,-0.2,\,-0.2,\,-0.2\,].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 8: Verification via circular convolution.</h6>

<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally we verify that <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\otimes a^{-1}=\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\otimes a^{-1}=\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=4</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ch1.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a\otimes b)[n]=\sum_{k=0}^{3}a[k]\;b[(n-k)\bmod 4]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a\otimes b)[n]=\sum_{k=0}^{3}a[k]\;b[(n-k)\bmod 4].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch1.Ex81X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex81X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(a\otimes a^{-1})[0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(a\otimes a^{-1})[0]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex81X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a[0]b[0]+a[1]b[3]+a[2]b[2]+a[3]b[1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a[0]b[0]+a[1]b[3]+a[2]b[2]+a[3]b[1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch1.Ex81Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex81Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\cdot 0.8+1\cdot(-0.2)+1\cdot(-0.2)+1\cdot(-0.2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\cdot 0.8+1\cdot(-0.2)+1\cdot(-0.2)+1\cdot(-0.2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch1.Ex81Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex81Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1.6-0.2-0.2-0.2=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1.6</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1.6-0.2-0.2-0.2=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Ch1.S10.SSx3.SSS0.Px8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ch1.Ex82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ch1.Ex82X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex82X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(a\otimes a^{-1})[1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(a\otimes a^{-1})[1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex82X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a[0]b[1]+a[1]b[0]+a[2]b[3]+a[3]b[2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a[0]b[1]+a[1]b[0]+a[2]b[3]+a[3]b[2]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch1.Ex82Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex82Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\cdot(-0.2)+1\cdot 0.8+1\cdot(-0.2)+1\cdot(-0.2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\cdot(-0.2)+1\cdot 0.8+1\cdot(-0.2)+1\cdot(-0.2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ch1.Ex82Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ch1.Ex82Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-0.4+0.8-0.2-0.2=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-0.4+0.8-0.2-0.2=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
